{
  "openapi" : "3.0.1",
  "info" : {
    "title" : "IVA Chat Bot API",
    "description" : "# Introduction\nIVA Chat Bot REST API provides functions which should used of 3-rd party chat bots.\n\nClients API is described [here](/doc/api/rest.html).\n\nServer to server integration API is described [here](/doc/api/integration.html).\n\n# Authentication\nAll requests to the system require authorization to perform a certain action. Such requests in the API description are marked with the - `AUTHORIZATIONS` marker.\n\n<SecurityDefinitions />\n\nAuthentication is performed using API key scheme, thereby all HTTP requests which are required authentication\nmust include an access token which must be sent in the `X-Iva-Bot-Api-Token` HTTP request header:\n\n    X-Iva-Bot-Api-Token: <botToken>\n\n# Get bot access token\nTo get bot access parameters (`<botToken>`) contact IVA system administrator which should create an account\nfor the bot and send back the access parameters.\n",
    "version" : "1.28.12"
  },
  "servers" : [ {
    "url" : "/api/rest/bot",
    "description" : "The stage API server"
  } ],
  "tags" : [ {
    "name" : "Requests",
    "description" : "## Method usage\n<table>\n  <tr><th>Method</th><th>Usage</th></tr>\n  <tr><td rowspan=4>POST</td><td>To create the resource</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>To complitely update the resource</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>To start the process</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>To remove from the collection all of elements with identifiers from the specified collection</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>GET</td><td>To get the resource</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>PATCH</td><td>To partialy update the resource</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>DELETE</td><td>To delete the resource by identifier</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n## Parameter passing\nFor all requests, identifiers are passed in the path, except sending a collection of them. In this case, identifiers can be sent as comma-separated query parameter for GET-method, or in the request body for POST-method.\n\nQuery parameters are sent only with a GET-method. In this case special symbols such as _ ,+, \\, #, &, %, \" must be encoded:\n<table>\n  <tr><th>Symbol</th><th>Encoding</th></tr>\n  <tr><td>Space</td><td>%20</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>!</td><td>%21</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>\"</td><td>%22</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>#</td><td>%23</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>$</td><td>%24</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>%</td><td>%25</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>&</td><td>%26</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>'</td><td>%27</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>(</td><td>%28</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>)</td><td>%29</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>*</td><td>%2A</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>+</td><td>%2B</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>,</td><td>%2C</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>-</td><td>%2D</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>.</td><td>%2E</td></tr>\n  <tr><td>/</td><td>%2F</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nArray query parameters are serialized by default using style: form and explode: true, resulting in repeated parameter names like /users?id=3&id=4&id=5.\n"
  }, {
    "name" : "Responses",
    "description" : "## HTTP status codes\nStandard HTTP response codes are used to identify the success of the request.\n<table>\n    <tr><th>HTTP response code</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n    <tr><td>200 - Ok</td><td>The request was successful and the data was returned in the response</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>204 - No content</td><td>The request was successful and there is no data in the response</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>400 - Bad Request</td><td>Some request parameters were passed incorrectly</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>401 - Unauthorized</td><td>Authentication data is missing or incorrect</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>403 - Forbidden</td><td>The request with the current authentication data is not allowed</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>404 - Not Found</td><td>The requested resource was not found</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>415 - Unsupported Media Type</td><td>The request was send with invalid Content-Type header</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>500 - Server Error</td><td>Unexpected server-side error</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n## Handling exception\nIf the response code differs from `200 - Ok` and `204 - No Content`, additional error information is passed in the response body:\n<SchemaDefinition schemaRef=\"#/components/schemas/ERROR\" exampleRef=\"#/components/examples/ERROR\"/>\n"
  } ],
  "paths" : {
    "/chats/{chatRoomId}/files/create" : {
      "post" : {
        "tags" : [ "Chat methods" ],
        "summary" : "Create resource",
        "description" : "Creates a file representation to bind with the file to be uploaded",
        "operationId" : "createResource",
        "parameters" : [ {
          "name" : "chatRoomId",
          "in" : "path",
          "description" : "Chat room ID",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "format" : "uuid"
          }
        } ],
        "requestBody" : {
          "description" : "A name of the resource",
          "content" : {
            "application/json" : {
              "schema" : {
                "$ref" : "#/components/schemas/CreateResourceWithSizeRestDTO"
              }
            }
          },
          "required" : true
        },
        "responses" : {
          "200" : {
            "description" : "An identifier of the resource",
            "content" : {
              "application/json" : {
                "schema" : {
                  "type" : "string",
                  "format" : "uuid"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400" : {
            "description" : "reason = FS_LIMIT_RESTRICTION, type = IvcsAccessControlException - There is no enough free space to upload file to specified context"
          }
        },
        "security" : [ {
          "BotApiToken" : [ ]
        } ]
      }
    },
    "/chats/{chatRoomId}/files/{resourceId}" : {
      "get" : {
        "tags" : [ "Chat methods" ],
        "summary" : "Download file",
        "description" : "Downloads specified resource file from server. Inside we compose the URL and redirect user to this URL.Optionally one can add width and height parameters in order to resize image resource to given size. <br>Bot application should support temporary redirect (HTTP code 307)",
        "operationId" : "downloadFile",
        "parameters" : [ {
          "name" : "chatRoomId",
          "in" : "path",
          "description" : "Chat room ID",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "format" : "uuid"
          }
        }, {
          "name" : "resourceId",
          "in" : "path",
          "description" : "Resource ID to download",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "format" : "uuid"
          }
        }, {
          "name" : "accessDeniedBehaviour",
          "in" : "query",
          "description" : "Whether server send stub picture instead of 403 error code in case of file access denied.",
          "schema" : {
            "$ref" : "#/components/schemas/ResourceAccessDeniedBehavior"
          }
        } ],
        "responses" : {
          "200" : {
            "description" : "Success",
            "headers" : {
              "X-IvcsError" : {
                "description" : "Contains errors related to application: <br/>reason = SCAN_ACCESS_DENIED - resource access denied because it has virus or dlp <br/>reason = SECURITY_LEVEL_ACCESS_DENIED - resource access denied because it requires higher security level <br/>reason = NETWORK_ACCESS_DENIED - resource access denied because of network configuration",
                "style" : "simple",
                "schema" : {
                  "type" : "string"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403" : {
            "description" : "Success",
            "headers" : {
              "X-IvcsError" : {
                "description" : "Contains errors related to application: <br/>reason = SCAN_ACCESS_DENIED - resource access denied because it has virus or dlp <br/>reason = SECURITY_LEVEL_ACCESS_DENIED - resource access denied because it requires higher security level <br/>reason = NETWORK_ACCESS_DENIED - resource access denied because of network configuration",
                "style" : "simple",
                "schema" : {
                  "type" : "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security" : [ {
          "BotApiToken" : [ ]
        } ]
      },
      "post" : {
        "tags" : [ "Chat methods" ],
        "summary" : "Upload file",
        "description" : "Uploads file on server. Place raw file inside HTTP POST body and specify headers: resourceSize, chunkBegin and chunkEnd.<br/>They define the offset of a transmitted part relative to original file in bytes.<br/>It means that if you have a big file then you can upload it in parts with multiple http requests.",
        "operationId" : "upload",
        "parameters" : [ {
          "name" : "chatRoomId",
          "in" : "path",
          "description" : "Chat room ID",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "format" : "uuid"
          }
        }, {
          "name" : "resourceId",
          "in" : "path",
          "description" : "An id of the resource that should be bound with uploading file",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "format" : "uuid"
          }
        }, {
          "name" : "chunkBegin",
          "in" : "header",
          "description" : "An index into the File indicating the first byte to include in the Chunk.",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "format" : "int64"
          }
        }, {
          "name" : "chunkEnd",
          "in" : "header",
          "description" : "An index into the File indicating the first byte that will <b>not</b> be included in the new Chunk",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "format" : "int64"
          }
        }, {
          "name" : "resourceSize",
          "in" : "header",
          "description" : "A size of the file in bytes",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "format" : "int64"
          }
        } ],
        "requestBody" : {
          "content" : {
            "application/octet-stream" : {
              "schema" : {
                "type" : "object"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses" : {
          "204" : {
            "description" : "The chunk was successfully written"
          },
          "400" : {
            "description" : "reason = FS_MAX_FILE_SIZE_RESTRICTION, type = IvcsAccessControlException - File for upload is too big <br/>reason = CANNOT_UPLOAD_NO_THREADS_TO_SCAN, type = AVScanException - File cannot be uploaded because there is no free resources to scan file <br/>reason = CANNOT_UPLOAD_VIRUS_DETECTED, type = AVScanException - Virus detected <br/>reason = CANNOT_UPLOAD_UNCHECKABLE_FILE, type = AVScanException - File cannot be uploaded because it cannot be scanned for virus <br/>reason = CANNOT_UPLOAD_SCAN_ENGINE_ERROR, type = AVScanException - File cannot be uploaded because there is error in virus scan engine <br/>"
          },
          "403" : {
            "description" : "reason = INSUFFICIENT_RIGHTS, type = IvcsAccessControlException - There is no rights to perform upload"
          }
        },
        "security" : [ {
          "BotApiToken" : [ ]
        } ]
      }
    },
    "/chats/{chatRoomId}/send-message" : {
      "post" : {
        "tags" : [ "Chat methods" ],
        "summary" : "Send message",
        "description" : "Sends new message to chat. This method can be also used for replying on another message. If message are sent with attachment that the one should be uploaded to the server before.",
        "operationId" : "sendMessage",
        "parameters" : [ {
          "name" : "chatRoomId",
          "in" : "path",
          "description" : "Chat room ID",
          "required" : true,
          "schema" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "format" : "uuid"
          }
        } ],
        "requestBody" : {
          "description" : "Message data",
          "content" : {
            "application/json" : {
              "schema" : {
                "$ref" : "#/components/schemas/ChatMessageToSaveBotRestDTO"
              }
            }
          },
          "required" : true
        },
        "responses" : {
          "200" : {
            "description" : "Created message",
            "content" : {
              "application/json" : {
                "schema" : {
                  "$ref" : "#/components/schemas/ChatRoomMessageBotRestDTO"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400" : {
            "description" : "reason = RESOURCE_ALREADY_USED, type = IvcsAccessControlException - If message has attachment with already used resource"
          }
        },
        "security" : [ {
          "BotApiToken" : [ ]
        } ]
      }
    },
    "/botEventsChannel/chats" : {
      "get" : {
        "tags" : [ "Chat events" ],
        "summary" : "Getting updates",
        "description" : "Now there is one way of receiving updates for your bot - webhooks. <br/>Webhook of your bot should be registered by IVA system administrator.<br/><br/>Since webhook is registered, whenever there is an update for the bot, we will send an HTTPS POST request to the specified URL, containing a JSON-serialized [BotEvent](#operation/botEvents). In case of an unsuccessful request, we will give up after a reasonable amount of attempts.<br/><br/>If you'd like to make sure that the event was sent by IVA, you can specify secret data during webhook registration. If specified, the request will contain a header `Iva-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` with the secret token as content.",
        "operationId" : "botEvents",
        "responses" : {
          "200" : {
            "description" : "Subscribed"
          }
        },
        "callbacks" : {
          "Bot event" : {
            "" : {
              "post" : {
                "summary" : "Bot event",
                "requestBody" : {
                  "content" : {
                    "*/*" : {
                      "schema" : {
                        "$ref" : "#/components/schemas/BotEvent"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                },
                "responses" : {
                  "200" : {
                    "$ref" : "#/components/responses/EventOk"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components" : {
    "schemas" : {
